From 5ace16f9f975d25fb6a188f932144b6b59abeb31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Currie <rob@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:43:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: TGeoManager::Export writes a geometry back as the ROOT
 file it came from

`roottest/root/io/geo` builds all eighteen of its geometries with
`TGeoManager::Import("<geom>.root")` and then exports each one, so
`Export` is asked to write a manager read from a file, not one made in
memory. Import kept only the tree xrdroot answers questions with; it now
keeps the file's own TGeoManager members - and the layouts that file
described its classes with - and `Export` writes them into a new file
which carries those descriptions, so ROOT reads the geometry back as the
one that went in. Verified with ROOT 6.40.04: e907's export re-imports to
16722 nodes / 360 volume UIDs, max level 7, voxelization retrieved.

A manager made in memory has no such record, and a `.xml` name asks for
the XML flavour of ROOT's file format, which xrdroot's writer does not
write: both are refused in full sentences naming the `.gdml` export that
works. The two tests that asserted the old refusal text now assert the
new one, each still requiring the what-to-do-instead; neither assertion is
weakened, the behaviour it describes changed.

Before: 18 export tests UNSUPPORTED, 3 PASS. After: 14 PASS, 7 TIMEOUT
(alice, ams, btev, cms_cmse, d0, lhcbfull, phenix) - the write is correct
but 103 s for e907's 16722 nodes and hours for alice's, which the next
round's speed work must fix (wdobjects._basic converts every scalar
member through numpy: 7.1M calls for e907).
